# Test: ddos-local drops a REMOTE (transit) victim on the netfilter FORWARD hook
# when forward-mitigation is on, and defers to flowspec (no on-host drop) when it
# is off -- the end-to-end proof of spec-ddos-direction-allowlist AC-10.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-ddos-test-infra AC-4 -- a flood at a remote, box-unowned
#            victim (203.0.113.9) is classified Direction=remote (classifyDirection
#            -> iface.AddressIsLocal false, detector.go:354-367) and, with
#            `ddos { local { forward-mitigation } }` on, ddos-local installs an nft
#            drop on the FORWARD hook (hookForDirection -> HookForward,
#            responder.go:160-168; chain rendered `type filter hook forward`).
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-ddos-test-infra AC-5 -- with forward-mitigation off the
#            responder installs NO on-host drop and logs the flowspec deferral
#            (responder.go:111-118).
# PREVENTS:  a transit victim silently getting an INPUT-hook drop (which cannot
#            touch forwarded traffic), or forward-mitigation being ignored.
#
# COMPLEMENTS (does not replace) the exhaustive hook-selection unit test
# TestLocalHookByDirection (internal/plugins/ddos/local/responder_test.go:179):
# this proves the same selection end to end, through a real flood and a kernel
# nft readback.
#
# STATUS: option=needs-linux; runs as root on the QEMU Alpine VM. The compiled
# setup fixture creates the veth pair, then the compiled root driver polls the
# daemon and kernel state without a blind sleep. The nft readback stays in that
# root driver, which the runner keeps privileged for exactly this
# (runner_exec.go:740-744); no `firewall {}` block
#   is declared, so ApplyAll autoloads nft on demand (registry.go:104-109) with
#   ddos-local as the sole nft driver (spec D-2).
#
#   Two attack generations are required and are the timing-sensitive part of this
#   test: AttackDetected/Characterized emit ONCE per generation at attack onset
#   (detector.go:310-333, characterize.go:138-160), so hookForDirection is
#   consulted only then. Phase A (forward-mitigation ON) drives one generation and
#   proves the FORWARD drop; the flood then stops and the attack CLEARS (the drop
#   is withdrawn), the config reloads with forward-mitigation OFF, and Phase B
#   drives a fresh generation that must defer. If a QEMU run shows the reload/
#   re-trigger is flaky, AC-5 can be split into a sibling `.ci`; AC-4 (the parent
#   AC-10 mandate) stands alone in Phase A.

# This test needs a fully privileged host, not merely Linux, and needs TWO
# distinct capability families.
#   - net-admin: the driver builds the transit topology with
#     `ip link add zdd0 type veth peer name zdd0p` (line 66) and addresses it.
#   - bpf (CAP_BPF + CAP_SYS_RESOURCE): the traffic-usage block below drives
#     rlimit.RemoveMemlock() + link.AttachTCX()
#     (internal/plugins/trafficusage/attach_linux.go:33,46).
# A bare needs-linux ran this on the unprivileged GitHub runner, where neither is
# available, so it could only fail (ai/rules/qemu-testing.md).
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf
# Serialize against every other ddos test: they all flood the SAME loopback
# interface and the detector picks the victim by top-destination-bytes over that
# interface, so a sibling's concurrent flood is indistinguishable from this
# test's own. Rationale in full: test/plugin/ddos-direction.ci.
option=exclusive:group=ddos-flood
option=env:var=ze.log.ddos.detect:value=info
option=env:var=ze.log.ddos.local:value=info
option=timeout:value=120s


stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
ddos {
	detect {
		enabled true
		absolute-floor 1000
		confirm-duration 1
		startup-grace 0
		baseline-window 10
		check-interval 1
		characterize-enable false
	}
	observe {
		incident-ring-size 100
	}
	local {
		response-level enforce
		forward-mitigation true
	}
}

traffic {
	usage {
		enabled true
		track-ip true
		interfaces {
			interface zdd0p {
				enabled true
			}
			interface zdd0 {
				enabled true
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/ddos-transit-forward-drop-setup
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/ddos-transit-forward-drop-driver:timeout=115s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=FORWARD-DROP-INSTALLED 203.0.113.9
expect=stdout:contains=REMOTE-DEFER-NO-DROP 203.0.113.9
expect=stderr:contains=ddos-local: drop rule installed
expect=stderr:contains=hook=forward
expect=stderr:contains=forward-mitigation disabled, deferring to flowspec
